A||||10||Gary W||Mystery pipe...||||5||
Z||000000||Gary W||10-22-2001||09:38 PM||||('86 GT 2.8) On the firewall side of my air cleaner box, there is a pipe fitting about 1/2" in diameter. A short hose connects this to a metal tube, which runs along the firewall to about the middle of the car, then...nothing - it's wide open. The manual shows this to be the fresh air inlet for the PCV system, but for that I have a formed/solid pipe from the front valve cover to the upstream side of the intake tube. Am I missing something?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-22-2001||09:43 PM||||This was part of the recall campaign and although it was disconnected, they were rarely removed.  Don't sweat it.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gary W||10-22-2001||09:46 PM||||Thanks - glad it's not something important.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||10-23-2001||05:46 PM||||That open pipe should really be capped.  Note that it runs to the outside of the air filter housing. This is the "filtered air" side (in a Fiero, air flows from the inside to the outside of the filter). You are essentially sucking unfiltered air thru that pipe into the engine.  Buy a rubber cap at any auto supply store (available from the HELP! line of products) and cap that pipe! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||10-23-2001||06:18 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Sooooooo thats what that pipe is, cool. Think I could just pinch it off?||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierobaby||10-23-2001||06:27 PM||||I was wounding about that stupid pipe too... the one I saw was capped though so I was even more confused!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gary W||10-23-2001||09:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mark:<BR><B>That open pipe should really be capped.  Note that it runs to the outside of the air filter housing. This is the "filtered air" side (in a Fiero, air flows from the inside to the outside of the filter). You are essentially sucking unfiltered air thru that pipe into the engine.  Buy a rubber cap at any auto supply store (available from the HELP! line of products) and cap that pipe! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn! Thanks for that, It went right by me that it was unfiltered air. I wonder how long it's been like that.||||reg||1
